  "narrative": {
    "top_frame": "JP Sears gave them a clean five innings. One hit, five strikeouts, no damage. And Manny Machado turned a tied game into a 5-2 lead with one swing late.",
    "what_this_means": "The margin was thin through six. Sears was doing the heavy lifting, but the lineup was stuck in neutral until the seventh inning arrived and suddenly felt like the only inning that mattered. That's when Machado drove in three runs and the game separated. The bullpen. Matsui, Rodriguez, Morejon, Miller. Held what the starter built and what the offense finally finished. Fernando Tatis Jr. went 3-for-5 and stayed involved, but it was Machado's moment that turned a close game into a result. The Dodgers scratched back twice, but not enough. This is a team that doesn't need to control early innings if the seventh inning shows up when it counts.",
    "what_to_watch": "Brandon Pfaadt and his 5.40 ERA face Walker Buehler tonight against an Arizona lineup that ranks among the weakest offenses in baseball. A matchup made for clean innings and room to work.",
